    "created_at": "2022-02-04T21:39:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-04T21:39:46Z",
    "body": "One scenario where a separate `asdf` module is useful: if (for example in the case of Python) you have a virtual environment installed with one version of Python, and then create a `.tool-versions` specifying a different local version of Python -- there are now two conflicting versions of Python in \"scope\" (`.venv/bin/python` and the `asdf` version). It would be great to highlight this discrepancy.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
